       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg, and a typical start is 2.5 to 5 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum and could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. It could also cause prolonged shock that is hard to reverse, because amlodipine has a long half-life.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, a common starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **Another dose**, if you give me the intended value\n\nIf 50 mg is deliberate, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
